WIDTH(1)  UNIX Programmer's Manual   WIDTH(1)

NAME
     width - filling, and the one word that
     will not fit

DESCRIPTION
     A paragraph is filled to whatever the
     measure is, and a word is never
     hyphenated: a manual page is full of
     tokens that must not break.

     So a word wider than the whole measure,
     supercalifragilisticexpialidociousandthensomemore,
     goes out over the right margin on a line
     of its own rather than in two pieces.

     A line block is not filled and runs past the margin exactly as it was written, however long it happens to be.
